DESIGN: The exact adult female FL FLAGELLANT A from the selected concept_v5b (NOT the older robed design): athletic, toned monk-like build, fair skin, natural face, dark brown hair in a messy high bun with a few short loose locks. A short crimson hooded capelet (#9E1F24) covering the shoulders and upper back, hood lying down behind the neck, fastened at the throat with a round iron clasp. A fitted crimson leather vest-corset with dark laces down the front over a white chemise; bare toned arms; the corset ends above a bare midriff in front only (the back is fully covered by the capelet and corset). A thick braided crimson rope sash knotted at the front of the waist with a single short thick tassel, a dark brown leather hip belt with thigh straps. Long crimson cloth panels hang from the sash at the front (to the knee) and back (to mid-shin), cut straight with a few large simple points, never thin tatters. Black fitted leggings, cream linen bandages wrapped around both shins, short dark brown heeled ankle boots with a strap. Black iron wrist cuffs on both wrists. Clean, broad hand-painted surfaces with strong dark fold shadows on the crimson cloth and lit ridges. No wounds, no blood, nothing hot touching the body. Key colours: crimson, black leggings #2A2526, cream #EDE3CF, iron #3A3A3E, brown leather #5A3A28, ember orange #E46A2A as painted colour only.
